  "body": "## Delivered scope\nA bounded companion to completed PR208. Derives affine population/reward composition, global proper-time/expansion moment rebasing and a contraction-based accumulated-reward error bound. Implements a fixed-grid closed-cut checkpoint and consumes two already-saved native panels. This is NOT B4 production restart, adaptive-controller recovery, or B3i physical calibration.\n\n## Actual evidence\n- Focused unit tests: 9/9; new manufactured-reference checks: 10/10; native saved-panel checks: 13/13.\n- Three actual JSON restarts at t=0.25,0.75,1.5 s are bitwise identical to the same uninterrupted global RK4 grid. Cumulative RHS work is retained.\n- N=256 state/reward errors: 2.06275796444e-9 / 6.09247763350e-10. Refinement ratios 17.4217,16.7121,16.3563 approach fourth order.\n- 2828 saved endpoint tags give 16968 panel-weighted values and 8484 summed comparisons. Counts and five sector energies agree within inherited conditional numerical bounds.\n- Native cut incoming/outgoing prefix: 5.6707393382004175 / 5.6853332194199175 per V0, with a new closed-form incoming primitive rather than old quadrature.\n- Wrong local-theta reweighting changes a saved gross tag by up to9870.41161794/V0. This is a saved-trajectory negative control, NOT a changed-clock native IVP. The QSS-reset future-count value1.25435955942e-22/V0 is an upper bound, NOT an observed correction.\n\n## Actual status and limitations\nCompleted stage outputs, publication and backup coverage: **18/20**. **R6 and C9 distinct-author reviews are NOT_RUN**. Native delegation was not exposed; serial checks and Wolfram CAS are not promoted to independent admission. No central promotion. Original canonical DAG record remains **28/88, delta0**, not a new full-DAG recount. Physical radii remain null and L4=false.\n\nThe historical seven-repository1406-branch/1037-PR metadata inventory was restored, then recent PRs and targeted HEADs were checked across seven repositories. This is not a fresh exhaustive read of every current branch or conversation transcript. Latest observed central HEAD22a99cb9b1691274e74c122d54521be4f2f51ba5 includes HE AZIMUTH09 on the CR native25 parent; central writes0.\n\n## Publication identities\n- Science/implementation S1: b8bd56bd5e54354dbe2a6617da33ec076467fe4e.\n- Delivery source D: ccd27140ebe4619d4ecf17b3192dd7676b0cdd36.\n- Final receipt F: 4d6e166cf9a644392a8a2b68c4c171a1fb658240.\n- All branch updates used expected SHA and force=false. This PR remains draft/open/unmerged.\n\n## Actual dual backup\nBASS_B3H_RESTART_D_20261028.zip: **4,877,921 bytes,66 members**, SHA256 **53d8a64625a0d8a57cef5e2d2c5461d84932d599f4467bc87bf1a639c3f0ebac**.\nDrive upload success plus separate metadata: **1cNtkW1pniZnu2n5taYqYwLmcEa_QBk8g**,4,877,921 bytes.\nDropbox upload completed plus separate metadata: **id:BSpOijBcT10AAAAAAEDIwQ**,rev **65ed9cdce3b740af03d47**,same bytes.\n\nLocal archive CRC and payload hashes were checked. The earlier endpoint D source was actually restored and its byte hash verified in this invocation. New checkpoint remote byte-hash readback is NOT claimed. Git contains code/tests/theory/report/handoff and selected summaries; the source ZIP also contains full raw results, figures, failure logs and pinned native inputs. D includes the explicitly declared post-publication receipt; F does not cause ZIP regeneration.\n\n## Execution and next obligation\nOne new combined study: child CPU3.174522s/wall3.234636562s. Total charged CPU33.14379s/wall100.994367028s includes conservative failed-launcher/startup debits, not exact whole-session elapsed totals. The plot permission failure, later nonfatal startup warning and intentional red tests are retained. Hash-only source guard repair did not rerun the science.\n\nNew native ODE0; new B3i RHS0; old tests/consume/plot/quadrature replay0. Execution allocation closed; unused arithmetic capacity is not new authority. Next obligation: one distinct-author saved-evidence R6/C9 review of this unit only. No new node, merge or central change is authorized. AUTO_NEXT_NODE=false.\n\n[Report](https://github.com/cosmosapjw-quantum/bass/blob/4d6e166cf9a644392a8a2b68c4c171a1fb658240/research/bass_b3h_restart_cocycle_20261028/REPORT_KO.md) · [Theory](https://github.com/cosmosapjw-quantum/bass/blob/4d6e166cf9a644392a8a2b68c4c171a1fb658240/research/bass_b3h_restart_cocycle_20261028/theory/RESTART_THEORY.md) · [Stage ledger](https://github.com/cosmosapjw-quantum/bass/blob/4d6e166cf9a644392a8a2b68c4c171a1fb658240/research/bass_b3h_restart_cocycle_20261028/STAGE_LEDGER.json) · [Actual final ACK](https://github.com/cosmosapjw-quantum/bass/blob/4d6e166cf9a644392a8a2b68c4c171a1fb658240/research/bass_b3h_restart_cocycle_20261028/delivery/FINAL_ROOT_ACK.json) · [Handoff](https://github.com/cosmosapjw-quantum/bass/blob/4d6e166cf9a644392a8a2b68c4c171a1fb658240/research/bass_b3h_restart_cocycle_20261028/HANDOFF_KO.md)",
